0 -10.4286 TD
(Writing a value to this register will immediately start a data transfer on the SER_TX pin.  If a)Tj
0 -1 TD
(UART write operation is pending, then the CPU will be blocked with wait states until the transfer)Tj
T*
(is complete before starting the new write operation.  This makes the UART transmit a relatively)Tj
T*
(expensive operation on the CPU, but avoids the necessity of buffering data and checking for)Tj
T*
(buffer overflow.  Reading a value from this register returns 255 \(0xff\) if no valid data byte is in)Tj
T*
(the receive buffer, and returns the value of the receive buffer otherwise, and clears the receive)Tj
T*
(buffer for additional reads.  Note that there is no FIFO associated with the UART.)Tj
38.7227 47.1771 TD
