-40.437 -4.0343 TD
(The external clock functions as the source clock for the entire processor.  On start-up, the processor)Tj
0 -1 TD
(runs at the same rate as the external clock.  The processor program may access the housekeeping)Tj
T*
(SPI to set the processor into PLL mode or DCO free-running mode.  In PLL mode, the external)Tj
T*
(clock is multiplied up by the feedback divider value to obtain the core clock.  In DCO mode, the)Tj
T*
(processor is driven by a trimmed free-running ring oscillator.)Tj
