(The counter/timer is a general-purpose 32-bit adder and subtractor that can be configured for a)Tj
0 -1 TD
(variety of timing functions including one-shot counts, continuous timing, and interval interrupts.  At a)Tj
T*
[(core clock rate of 80)-68.6(MHz, the longest single time interval is 26.84 seconds.)]TJ
1.7029 -28.2857 TD
(The value in this register is the current value of the counter.  Value is 32 bits.   The)Tj
0 -1 TD
(register is read-write and can be used to reset the timer.)Tj
0 -9.8571 TD
(The value in this register is the reset value for the comparator.)Tj
-1.7143 -13.2743 TD
(Note:  When the counter/timer is disabled, the reg_timer_value remains unchanged, which puts the)Tj
0 -1 TD
(timer in a hold state.  When re-enabled, counting resumes.  To reset the timer, write zero to the)Tj
T*
(reg_timer_value register.)Tj
0 12.9886 TD
(When enabled, the counter counts up or down from the value set in reg_timer_value at the time)Tj
0 -1 TD
(the counter is enabled.  If counting up, the count continues until the counter reaches reg_timer_data.)Tj
T*
(If counting down, the count continues until the counter reaches zero.)Tj
-0.0571 -6 TD
(In one-shot mode, the counter triggers an interrupt \(IRQ channel 10;  see next page\) when it)Tj
0 -1 TD
(reaches the value of reg_timer_data \(up count\) or zero \(down count\), and stops.)Tj
0.0571 5 TD
(In continuous mode, the counter resets to zero if counting up, and resets to the value in)Tj
0 -1 TD
(reg_timer_data if counting down, and the count continues immediately.  If the interrupt is enabled,)Tj
T*
(the counter will generate an interrupt on every cycle.)Tj
